\f0\fs22 \cf2 Colonel Tom Porker had been tethered to the roof of Parliament House of the Elvis, formerly the Clambake bordello. There were no funds allocated to keeping its fog machine going, so Colonel Tom\'92s cigar hung cold and unsmoked from his huge piggy mouth, which was an unfortunate image from any angle.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
