\f0\fs22 The pre-inauguration party had been underway for some hours before the Holy Momma and the Holy Aunts arrived. Kathy carried Sarah\'92s favourite office chair\'97the one she\'92d adjusted all the heights, tilts, lumber supports and angles over several months until the feeling of her internal organs being squashed to pancake batter by the little lodger inside her had been dialled down to barely sufferable. Kathy wheeled the chair through the crowd in the main barroom where two picnic chairs flanked the Holy Thrones of partly melted bobbleheads, gilt trimmings oceanic velvet and no padding to speak of. They had been trucked back from The Domain on Monday. Kathy kicked over the Throne of the Holy Momma, hoiked the office chair onto the dais and set it in the  throne\'92s place, while Hayley moved the picnic chair on the Great Teacher\'92s side over to where she and Kathy cold sit together during the ceremony.\
Sarah sat immediately and sighed in the pleasure of taking her weight off her feet. Hayley stood by Sarah and cased the room while Kathy went to the bar to fetch a glass of water for Sarah, and stiff bourbons for Hayley and herself.\
Walter, the ex-mayor of the now defunct 
\fs20 GET BENT
\fs22  movement, emerged  from the milling of guests, and sat in the Great Teacher\'92s throne . He was wearing a shirt with a collar, and was clutching a rolled-up festival poster in his fist; he had been holding it the same way for forty minutes. Sarah placed a hand on his, even though the kid showed no signs he was shaken by the deaths of so many Elvi. But the poster in Walter\'92s hand had been signed personally by the original High Elvis, Walter was holding it as kind of totem of life and death, and Sarah simply missed the signs.\
Hayley waved away  the bourbon with a kind of on-duty officiousness. Kathy shrugged, sat down and drank both in single gulps.\
\'93I\'92ll get drunk just kissing you,\'94 Hayley said.\
Kathy giggled. \'93It\'92s good to know I have that affect on you.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f0\fs22 Chanta among the gathering, somewhat hampered by the ceremonial sunglasses he was required to wear and the light reflecting of his ceremonial sash. He saw Sarah resting in an office chair, chatting with that urchin she seemed to taking a liking to.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f0\fs22 He felt\'85 well, awkward. He\'92d been surrounded by survivors of the sickness that struck so many Elvi at 
\fs20 GET BENT
\fs22 . He\'92d never felt the need to say anything important before, and regarded the need now as the kind of hassle he\'92d only ever felt in conversations with estranged relatives at UNSAC Day marches. He gravitated towards Elvi he knew; people who knew him would expect nothing from him. Mostly, that meant Elvines he\'92d slept with, which created a whole other dimension of awkward as the Elvines eyed off his entourage of Elvisettes (only the Great Teacher was allowed to invite Elvisettes). Most of them turned out to have been at Bent Street too, which added yet another dimension of awkward as they seemed to expect some consoling words from him as Great Teacher. Strangely, his offers to hook up later just seemed to make things worse.\
Chanta searched his low-performing skull for the words that any decent great teacher might say at times like these, and come up with, \'93Evolution will work it out in the end.\'94\
\'93Praise the Dawkins,\'94 one mourner intoned.\
\'93And the One After the One,\'94 into another.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 We won\'92t praise the Dawkins
\f0\i0 , Chanta muttered under his breath. Fortunately no one heard him; that was an argument even Chanta could figure out had passed beyond his winning.\
Awkward.\
Chanta was saved by the Chief of Staff of the High Elvis-elect circulating among the guests, followed by a noticeable drift trending to a crush of guests at the bar. \'93If everyone cold take their places,\'94 the Chief of Staff said. \'93We\'92re about to begin.\'94 She noticed Chanta\'92s pained looked at the standing room only between him and a drink, and put her hand on his shoulder. \'93I\'92ll make sure we send over something nice,\'94 she reassured and smiled.\
Walter was still in Chanta\'92s throne, casting out territorial stare that said, 
\f2\i I\'92m the mayor of GET BENT, and I don\'92t care even if you are the Great Preacher or whatever they call you.
\f0\i0 \
Chanta waved the kid\'92s resting Fight Club face down. \'93Stay, there,\'94 he said, and sat on the edge of the dais. It was about as close to Sarah as he could get without his limbs turning to jack cheese, and it allowed his Elvisettes to huddle closer. Some sat on the dais; some sat on the floor at his feet. Tax! One removed his shoes and massaged his feet. He was glad he\'92d changed his socks that morning.\
The house lights went down and three spots focussed on the spa bath where a Clambake-series Elvis called Tom Wilson climbed two wooden steps that had been screwed to the side of the spa bath and stood on the mosaics, where the mermaids had been looking world-weary since before anybody in the room was born.\
\'93My fellow Elvi,\'94 Tom said. \'93Praise the Dawkins.\'94\

\f2\i Praise the Dawkins! Bless the Holy Momma!\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0 \cf2 Chant ground his teeth.
\f2\i \

\f0\i0 \'93We are all equal under Evolution,\'94 Tom declared. \'93The Airborne, the Cloudborne, and the descendants of the clones. We are the survivors, we are the fittest.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 We are the survivors, we are the fittest. It is meet and right to be so.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0 \cf2 \'93I give you a solemn promise, in this tragic time of the passing of the first High Elvis of the Elvi of Ulyssia. I promise to never deviate from the vision of my predecessor; I will make it my life\'92s work walk in the shoes of him whose suede shoes I am perfectly fit to tie because, like him, I am a Clambake Elvis through and through.\'94\
Cheers went of from the crowd.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Long live the High Elvis! Long live the Clambakes!\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0 \cf2 \'93Thank you very much. I also want to announce the second Parliament of the Elvi have, this morning decreed, in honour of teh first High Elvis, that every elected successor to this lofty office shall be a Clambake Elvis. I am but the second of the Clambake Dynasty.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Clambake! Dynasty! Dynasty!\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0 \cf2 With genuine humility, the kind that only a true Elvis could summon up, Tom hushed them down. \'93We have work to do, fellow Elvi. We are threatened. We are threatened by disease, and we are threatened by schism in our own kind. The Holy Rollers have forsaken the Oath of the Warranty and are being consumed by gospel music, exactly as we were warned against. Our warranty cards are our guising light Evolution takes our emancipation generations ago and teaches us that we are fit to be here because we 
\f2\i are
\f0\i0  here.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 We are here! You are here! I am here!
\f0\i0  
\f2\i \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0 \cf2 \'93I solemnly pledge that I will strive tirelessly to heal the schism of the Holy Rollers, we will follow the teachings of Evolution, we will give thanks to the Dawkins. We will give thanks that the scales have been removed from our eyes, and now we can see.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 We can see! We can see!
\f0\i0 \
\'93Evolution teaches us to throw off the shackles of Latter Day Capitalism. We reject the false belief that you can measure the virtue of a human being by the size of their off-shore investments.\'94\

\f2\i Off shore! Off shore!
\f0\i0 \
\'93And we look forward to the second coming the Dawkins, delivered to us by the Holy Momma.\'94\
And the people sang:\
