\f0\fs22 Chanta ground his teeth. If those Sages wrote one more song, he\'92d have to send them back to Grease or whatever movie set they came from. He was reasonably sure Fisher kept an account for making people disappear; in fact Fisher was curious as to why Chanta hadn\'92t made anyone disappear yet.
\f2\i \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0 \cf2 Tom Wilson, second High Elvis of the Elvi of Ulyssia, went on, \'93but even as we mourn the passing of the first Elvis, even as we remember how he used to sing \'91I\'92ll shower never\'92 in the bathroom every morning, we must move on from this tragedy. There is no time for crying in the ghetto, for there is promised land awaiting us. We must be brave because we don\'92t have a pudding heart. We\'92ll shower ever, brothers and sisters, and the fair is moving on.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Clean the Domain! Clean the Domain!
\f0\i0 \
\'93That was the other one,\'94 Tom chuckled and flashed his famous smile. \'93But I\'92ll take it.\'94
\f2\i \
