\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 The ceremony ended and the room did not empty, because nothing in the Clambake ever emptied. It redistributed. It turned from a room facing one way into a room facing every way at once, and the two currents that mattered ran between the spa bath and the bar and met head on in the middle, so that anybody carrying a full glass through the crossing was carrying a wet shirt home.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 It was a celebration and it was a wake and nobody had told the room which one to be, so it was being both, a few metres apart. Two Blue Hawaiis laughed until one had to take hold of the other\u8217 ?s sleeve to stay upright. Close enough to touch them, a Tulsa wept into a beer with somebody\u8217 ?s hand flat on the back of his neck, and neither party found the other odd.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Sarah stayed in the chair. Standing up was a project with stages and an audience, and there was no need for it, because the room came to her. It came in ones and twos and stood in something that was not quite a queue and would have been offended to be called one. They wanted the belly. Every second one asked first and every fourth one cried, and Sarah, who had two centuries of practice at being looked at, said thank you and thank you and thank you.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Which freed the Holy Aunts entirely, and they took the freedom.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 The High Elvis came over before the crowd could get to him. He came without the Chief of Staff, and he came up the two steps of the dais with his hand already out, and he said the correct thing about the Holy Momma\u8217 ?s health in the correct voice, and Sarah said the correct thing back.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Walter stood up out of the Great Teacher\u8217 ?s throne with the poster in his fist.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 He did not ask. He held it out with both hands the way you hand over something at a counter, and the High Elvis looked at it for a moment and then took it and unrolled it against the balustrade. It was the Rock Against Revival bill, four thousand names down the back of it in six-point type, and one of them was his, and across the top of it there was already a signature.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 The High Elvis looked at that for slightly longer.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Then he took a pen off a passing Elvis without asking for it, and signed his name underneath, and rolled it up and handed it back, and said, \u8220 ?Thank you very much,\u8221 ? and went down into the room.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Walter unrolled it again and held it up to the light of the busted chandelier.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 It was the same one.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 He rolled it back up and did not show anybody, and held it the way he had been holding it all night, and sat down again in a throne that was not his.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy went into the crowd.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Hayley went with her as far as the stairs and then went up them, because she had spent a career in rooms and had never once learned anything from the middle of one. From the floor you could see a wall of people. From the mezzanine you could see where the wall opened.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 It opened for the Great Teacher.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 That was the thing you could not miss from up there and could not see at all from down in it. He came out of the crush with his sunglasses throwing light at the ceiling and the room folded off him the way water goes off a bow, and closed up behind him \u8212 ? but it did not close on everybody. There was a wake. People came through in it and were let through, and the same wake went back across the floor a few minutes later, and then again.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy watched the third of these from beside the bar with a drink she was not drinking.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 He was going back and forth because he could not keep hold of a beer. He had two, and the crossing was too tight to get two through it, so he put them down his neck where he stood rather than wear them \u8212 ? and then he was a man with nothing in his hands, at a bar he had just left. And nobody would let him buy his own. That was the whole engine of it. Every Elvis between the dais and the taps wanted the honour, so the moment he arrived he had two again, and the moment he tried to sit down he had to get rid of them, and the thing wound him back and forth across that floor all night like a toy on a track.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 The people in his wake were not the same people every time. Kathy noticed it on the fourth crossing and then could not stop noticing it. Somebody would peel off at the bar and stay there talking; two others would attach on the way back; and there were faces going across with him now that had been standing by the curtains since the start.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 She was a doctor at a party, so she circulated, and what she was actually doing was getting sleeves pushed up.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 A Clambake with grey coming through his sideburns got himself off the chesterfield in three separate movements, with a hand on the arm of it and a noise. Two paces further on an Elvine came off a bar stool and stood a moment with her palm pressed flat into the small of her back, waiting for something to finish. Nobody looked at either of them. In that room it was weather.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Then Rusty Martin came off a low stool in one go, still talking, and went to the bar.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy did not stop walking. Her head turned, though, and stayed turned a beat past where it had any business.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Maile Duval had her sleeve pushed up past the elbow and her arm out and a small audience for it, and she was delighted with herself.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?[ ] years,\u8221 ? she was saying. \u8220 ?[ ] years I\u8217 ?ve had that, and I went to a man in Bent Street about taking it off and he told me it\u8217 ?d cost more than the wedding did.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Let me,\u8221 ? said Kathy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Maile put the arm into her hands with the satisfaction of a woman who has finally found somebody qualified to agree with her. There had been a name on the inside of that forearm once, done in the ornate lettering that takes a good hand and a long sitting. It was a grey suggestion now. The heavy work at the edges had held on better than the rest, so what was left was an outline with the middle gone out of it, like a word rubbed off a blackboard by somebody in a hurry.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?When did it start going?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?That\u8217 ?s what I can\u8217 ?t tell you. I looked at his name every morning of my life, and then one morning I\u8217 ?m at the sink and I think, hang on.\u8221 ? She turned the wrist over. \u8220 ?Best thing that\u8217 ?s happened to me all year, and I\u8217 ?m counting walking out of Bent Street.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy turned the arm into the light off the bar and did not let go of it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Any scars?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?What?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Anything you\u8217 ?ve had a long time. Old ones.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Maile thought about it, and pushed the sleeve the rest of the way up, to a place above the elbow where there was nothing whatever to see, and looked at the nothing for a while with a different face on.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Huh,\u8221 ? she said.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy gave the arm back, gently, and was already looking past her, because it was not the same on all of them. The woman beside Maile had a forearm you could still read. Dianne Carter, two along, had one you would have to be told was there at all. Some of them were further into whatever this was than the others, and there was nothing in a single face in that group to tell you which.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Dianne Carter had been watching her do it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Go on then,\u8221 ? she said.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?I\u8217 ?m not doing anything.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?You\u8217 ?re doing something.\u8221 ? She was not shouting, and it was worse than shouting. \u8220 ?Do you know what I\u8217 ?ve been doing since Bent Street? Going to funerals in perfect health. I\u8217 ?ve been the healthiest thing at [ ] of them. Cousins of mine are in the ground and I have never felt better in my life and nobody will tell me why, and now here\u8217 ?s Aunt Kathy going up and down the room looking at everybody\u8217 ?s arms.\u8221 ? She held her own out, palm up. \u8220 ?So go on. Is it us? Are we next?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy had never in her life pretended to an answer she did not have, so she took the arm and looked at it properly, and what she found in the crook of it was skin like the inside of a shell.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Across the floor the crowd opened again, and the Great Teacher came through it towards the curtains with two beers he had not asked for and his wake behind him, and stopped in front of the group, and looked at all their faces, and reached for something consoling.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?You\u8217 ?re all looking well,\u8221 ? said Chanta.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 It went down like a dropped tray.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy watched him try to get out from under it, and fail, and retreat into the beer, and take his wake back across the floor towards the dais.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Then she followed him.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 He had got himself onto the edge of the dais with the Elvisettes settling round him, some on the boards and some on the floor at his feet, and one of them had his shoes off again. Sarah was above him in the chair with her hands on the belly. Walter was in the throne with the poster. Hayley came down off the stairs and stood at the end of the dais where she could see the room.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Those Elvines you were talking to,\u8221 ? said Kathy. \u8220 ?You know them?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Sure. I know a lot of Elvines, Kathy.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?They\u8217 ?re looking well.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Chanta nodded. \u8220 ?I guess I just make them happy. They say I make them laugh.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy had to credit that. People did tend to laugh around Chanta. \u8220 ?How many of them have you laughed all the way into bed?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Kathy, are you jealous?\u8221 ?\
